[Music]  6 42  time for our morning cup of joe with  metro sheriff joe lombardo good morning  to you sheriff it's great to see you  hi alex hello uh we want to start with  this question sheriff there have been a  lot of burglaries recently on the west  side of town people are stealing  appliances from new homes before people  are moving into those homes so  do you have any suspect info at this  point and are they reselling those  appliances  yeah i wish i knew what they were doing  with them you know what we've  experienced  in the past and our you know police  knowledge on these kind of events  is they tend to take them out of state  and use different websites to get rid of  them  and or i guess you call them fences to  get rid of the stolen property  and more often than not they end up in  mexico so  there's a whole plethora of ways that  people can get rid of those  ill-gained items but in particular to  our issue we've had 27 plus  separate burglaries occur and they've  occurred mostly on the weekends  so if you are living adjacent to a new  home development  or you're living in the new home  development and houses are currently  under construction we ask the public to  be aware of this so the suspect  description on these is a  silver f-150 truck extended cab truck  and it occurs during the evening hours  on the weekends  and the truck would pull up to the front  of the house  they gain entry to the house and  set up their appliances by removing them  for wherever they're there they are in  the house  and set it up for another truck to come  by at a later period  and this is a big white panel truck that  backs into the driveway  and they put the appliances in that  truck and drive away  so i'm hoping there's somebody out there  in the public that'll see this  occurring and call us because right now  that's the most we have as far as leads  it's been posted on crime stoppers  385-5555  if you have the information and you want  to provide it  with anonymity associated with it if  it's more pressing like it's occurring  right in front of you  i i suggest you call 9-1-1 or 3-1-1 so  we can get there right away to  to address the issue yeah we have those  pictures of those vehicles for you to on  our website gosh the last thing you want  when you move into your new house is  your appliance is gone  all right yeah interesting enough we  have one of my my employees direct  employees that  that occurred to them they were getting  ready to move in the house next day and  they get in there and the house was  flooded because they separated the  refrigerator from the water system  and subsequently set them back a few  weeks so that's a big deal  how awful all right call crime stoppers  if you have any information  last week sheriff your officers were on  a call they were talking to a citizen  when someone started  shooting at them luckily they were not  hurt but obviously this is very  concerning  so when something like that happens does  metro implement any training or any  changes  yeah i mean that's a that's a great  question because it would be ignorant or  malpractice if we did  do something when we're aware of  something occurring we didn't make  adjustments in our training or how we  respond to calls  so similar to like one october it would  be malpractice if we didn't learn  something  from our failures there and then just  how we operate so in this case  officers were on a independent call  for service an illegal shooting and they  were standing out in front of the  residence that was associated with the  call uh having a conversation with the  resident  of that place and subsequently they had  shots fired upon them  um luckily they weren't hit um  and they were able to return fire and  get a good description of the suspect  and because of a good police work in the  proceeding 24 hours an individual  officer who had knowledge  of the description of the suspect was  able to locate him  and we obtained a confession  but a bigger picture is to your question  do we do we learn from these type of  incidents do we adjust our training so  they don't occur in the future  yes absolutely and you heard us talk  about the  reality-based training facility that  we're proposing  out in the northeast part of town so  officers  on these low frequency high risk events  we could put them in training scenarios  to adjust their  mo or how they respond to these type of  calls in the future  so they they meet them with success and  without getting harmed  uh it's important for us to learn from  our mistakes and  move forward from yeah i'm glad your  officers weren't hurt in that  allegiant stadium can now have a limited  number of fans some really good news  uh but sheriff a big question has been  parking so  when a game or event does happen how  will metro be enforcing traffic around  the stadium there's going to be a lot of  it  yeah um well here's um the only silver  lining of this pandemic  is is we've had ability to take our time  and ensure that we have proper protocols  in place  um to address these kind of situations  so the the traffic control company is a  private company that we partner with  to control the traffic in and out of the  stadium and this company is currently  contracted with t-mobile so they have  some experience working with us they  have some experience with the las vegas  community  and the ingress egress different routes  of  a big stadium like this so they put a  lot of protocols in place in partnership  with us  and and with it being a limited capacity  event  we'll be able to work all through all  the faults and nuances and everything  that you can imagine on a type of event  like this of its breadth and size  we can slowly work our way into it and  figure out where the  issues are with the people coming in and  out  so that was a long convoluted answer to  a simple problem  and the simple problem is we're used to  it we've done it the company we're  partnering with  has done it at other stadiums throughout  the united states  in particular to the nfl and i think  we'll meet success  uh with our plan yeah we'll be nice to  get fans in there too at some point all  right  sheriff thank you for being with us it  is great to see you you're welcome good  to see  you all right if you at home have a  question for sheriff joe lombardo  send it to us on our website  eightnewsnow.com and find out if your  question was answered  every wednesday

